<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Foraker Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1900</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Foraker Act was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> law of April 1900 that set up civil government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>. It provided for a governor and executive council appointed by the US president and an elected house of delegates, but did not grant Puerto Ricans US citizenship. It was replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jones-shafroth-act">Jones Act of 1917</a>.</p></div>
